## Inline notes / decisions worth carrying forward

- **`createPluginManager` is async** — returns `Promise<PluginManager>`. Callers must `await`. Documented in TRD §2.3 (revision noted in TRD itself).
- **Atomic rollback pattern** (applyManifest): wrap `capabilityRegistry.register()` in try/catch; on failure, restore `existing` to the store and re-save. Don't trust the registry's own collision check as a guarantee — wrap it anyway.
- **`PLUGIN_CLEANUP_TIMEOUT` is a console warning only**, not a stored `lastError`. The record is removed immediately after, so a `lastError` field would be invisible. Documented in TRD.
- **`installFromRegistry()` always throws `PLUGIN_MARKETPLACE_UNAVAILABLE`** until the marketplace pack ships. Body is the API seam — no other code path touches it.
- **Plugin type → CapabilityType**: `runtime` → `runtime`; `service`/`developer` → `platform`. Aligns with docs' permission tiering.
- **CapabilityRecord `owner` field** is required by the registry even though the registry overrides it with the function param. Always include `owner` when pre-registering capabilities in tests or when building records.
- **System clock** uses `@ts-expect-error` on Node's `setTimeout` (returns `Timeout`, `Clock` declares `number`). Two packages affected: `plugin-manager` and `session-manager` (committed in `66d4362`).
- **`YamlValue` recursive type** replaces `unknown` to satisfy the project's banned-types check. Defined in `plugin-manager/src/types.ts`.

## Next pack (Tier 2, #5)

**`gateway-core`** — Auth, session creation, capability discovery, routing to a runtime. No execution logic.

- **Depends on**: Tier 1 complete ✓ (now true)
- **Source doc**: Agentide → Section 9; Terminology → Control Plane
- **First real consumer** of `@platform/plugin-manager` — will subscribe to `plugin.*` events (the events bus doesn't have any subscribers yet on the platform side)
- **Will also wire up** `@platform/session-manager` and `@platform/capability-registry` as the three core control-plane components

Parallel opportunity once gateway-core lands: `sdk-node` (#8) and `mcp-adapter` (#9) don't block each other.

